  "tagline": "Embedded in-memory and hybrid database for devices, real-time systems and time-series analytics.",
  "description": "eXtremeDB from McObject is a small-footprint embedded database that runs in-process on everything from microcontrollers and real-time operating systems to large servers, with in-memory, persistent or hybrid storage per table. Beyond classic embedded use in telecom, aerospace and industrial control, it offers columnar \"sequences\" for time-series analytics, which made it popular for market data in its Financial Edition, along with SQL, clustering and high availability. The eXtremeDB/rt variant targets hard real-time systems with deadline-aware transactions. Version 9.0 (July 2026) added native approximate-nearest-neighbour indexes and an ultra-lightweight edge client. It is proprietary and licensed per product.",
